cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these tables, please cite them and the work of Antieau, Krause and Nikolaus on
  which the computation rests.
title: "FiniteChainSyntomicCohomology: p-adic K-groups of Z/p^n in degrees up to 100"
abstract: >-
  The p-adic K-groups K_r(Z/p^n; Z_p), 1 <= r <= 100, of the 19 rings Z/p^n tabulated in
  Appendix A of Antieau, Krause and Nikolaus, On the K-theory of Z/p^n, computed with
  Syntomic.jl, with the groups that are new relative to that appendix marked.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Ong
    given-names: Wern Juin Gabriel
    email: gabriel_ong@ieee.org
repository-code: "https://github.com/wgabrielong/FiniteChainSyntomicCohomology"
keywords:
  - algebraic K-theory
  - syntomic cohomology
  - finite chain rings
references:
  - type: article
    title: "On the K-theory of Z/p^n"
    authors:
      - family-names: Antieau
        given-names: Benjamin
      - family-names: Krause
        given-names: Achim
      - family-names: Nikolaus
        given-names: Thomas
    identifiers:
      - type: other
        value: "arXiv:2405.04329"
  - type: software
    title: "Syntomic.jl: syntomic cohomology and K-theory of finite chain rings"
    authors:
      - family-names: Ong
        given-names: Gabriel
    url: "https://github.com/wgabrielong/Syntomic.jl"
